ocalisation (steps 06\u201311):** 1006's activity is confined to three bursts: ~20431\u201321630, ~37632\u201337731 / ~41232\u201341331, and ~46832\u201347431. Step_12 shows the 41232 event is *incoming*, and step_14 shows all three early out-contacts (45, 230, 925) fall in [20431, 21630]. 1860's *incoming* contacts occur at ~19831\u201320430, ~26432\u201327031, ~32432\u201333631, ~36632\u201336931, and ~43432\u201343631 (step_13: from 153). 1860 has **no events after 46831**, so 1006's last out-burst cannot reach it at all.\n\n**Gap arithmetic:** the only orderings that could work are 1006-out \u224821000 \u2192 1860-in \u224826400+ (\u0394 \u2265 5,300) or 1006-out \u224837700 \u2192 1860-in \u224843500 (\u0394 \u2248 5,800). With a 600-unit maximum inter-hop delay these require \u226510 and up to ~37 consecutive relays.\n\n**Relay-capacity control (steps 15, 16):** in the 600-unit neighbourhoods, relays are thin \u2014 230 has 1 event, 925 has 2, 1532 has 1, 1680 has 3 around 1006's burst; on the target side only 153 is busy (8 events) while 182, 743, 958, 1390 are completely silent in [42832, 43631]. With ~3.5 events per node across 38,400 time units, a typical node re-emits within 600 units with only ~5% probability, so the branching factor of a 600-unit-constrained cascade is strongly sub-critical. A chain persisting 5,000+ time units is not supported by the observed activity.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_68f9c03d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860, 45, 153, 230, 925, 1532, 1680],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.66,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", 